# Graphify — exactly three artifacts are tracked: graph.json (the artifact a
# query reads), graph.html and GRAPH_REPORT.md. Everything else under
# graphify-out/ is local, including the exploration record:
#   memory/      one file per saved exploration (question + verified answer)
#   reflections/ LESSONS.md, deterministically generated from memory/
#   findings/    the judge decision log
# Those three are the agent working layer (below) — they are written by
# untracked tooling, describe the unshipped `.agents/` tree, and are not a
# shared map of this codebase.
graphify-out/cache/
graphify-out/manifest.json
graphify-out/cost.json
graphify-out/wiki/
graphify-out/.graphify_*
# Derived exports are regenerable and no longer produced by default (see
# scripts/graphify/graphify.sh: exports are opt-in via --export). They are ignored
# anyway so that running `export` once cannot stage tens of megabytes of
# wiki/, obsidian/, svg or callflow HTML.
graphify-out/obsidian/
graphify-out/graph.svg
graphify-out/GRAPH_TREE.html
graphify-out/*-callflow.html
graphify-out/20[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]/
graphify-out/memory/
graphify-out/reflections/
# Rebuild runtime state: rewritten or removed by the post-commit hook.
graphify-out/.pending_changes
graphify-out/.rebuild.lock

# Agent working layer: the review backlog and the judge decision log are
# produced by tooling that is itself untracked (.agents/scripts/judge-harness.mjs,
# .agents/rules/), so a reader cannot check a verdict against the rule that
# produced it. They stay on disk and keep feeding local agents; they are not
# part of what this repository publishes.
docs/
graphify-out/findings/

# Agent Runtime, Harness & Workspace State (per-developer, never shared)
/.agent
/.agents
/.omp
/.codex
/conductor
/AGENTS.md
**/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
**/.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
**/.claude/routines/.state/
**/.claude/worktrees/
**/.claude/checkpoints/
**/.claude/mailbox/
**/.claude/agent-registry.json
**/.claude/agent-memory-local
**/.claude/first-run
**/.claude/assistant-daemon-state.debug

# Interpreter path recorded per machine by `graphify hook install`; the hooks
# themselves are tracked, so the value has to live outside them.
/.husky/.graphify-python

.worktrees/

# CDP Heap Snapshots & Network Traces (browser-testing skill output)
# The file globs cover any output directory, so no per-directory entries are
# needed — `docs/heap-snapshots/` and `docs/har/` were left behind by 319cc65
# and have not existed since.
*.heapsnapshot
*.heaptimeline
*.har
*.har.gz

# Environment & Secrets
.env
.env.local
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
!.env.template
*.pem
*.key

# Local Python/Graphify Environment Declarations (per-developer)
/pyproject.toml
/uv.lock

# Local Review Snapshots (do not hide unrelated project patch files)
/patch.diff
/full_patch.diff
